module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.declared_refusal_unreachable_from_its_own_constructor

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data declared_refusal_unreachable_from_its_own_constructor: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "declared_refusal_unreachable_from_its_own_constructor" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a refusal arm whose ONLY constructor implies the state that makes the arm unreachable is green on a shape no run can produce, and the type then reads as the wall it is not** (INVALID STATE: a coproduct declares a refusal cause; witnesses construct it directly and pass; and on the production path the thing that BUILDS its precondition also forces a different, earlier-matched arm, so the cause is never emitted. RECOGNITION RULE: for each declared refusal, name what constructs its precondition ON THE ACCEPTANCE PATH and check that nothing earlier in the match order shadows it -- the tell is that every green reading of the arm comes from a fixture the entry point cannot assemble. WHY IT IS WORSE THAN AN ABSENT ARM: a declared cause gets CITED AS COVERAGE, and a module can claim it as the wall protecting hardware while the acceptance path cannot express its red, which is DESIGN section 4b(1) rung inflation stated in the vocabulary of a type. THREE INSTANCES IN ONE LANE, gunbc#10739, which is what makes it a class rather than a coincidence: NoPeerAvailable was declared and matched but never constructed, because the fold mapped over an empty peer roster and contributed ZERO selections -- and zero selections is not a refused selection, it is nothing at all; the observer-identity arms ObserverIsTheSubjectMachine and ObserverHostnameNotConverged were reachable only from fixtures because the entry keyed itself on `hostname -s`, so a mislabelled runner failed the assignment lookup FIRST and never reached the identity check; and SubjectWasNotUpBeforeIssuance was unreachable because a refused pre-issuance baseline is its only constructor AND implies nothing was written, so the mint paired it with ResetNotAttempted while the verdict matched acknowledgement before observation. THE THIRD IS THE PUREST FORM: the precondition and the shadowing state are the SAME FACT, so no amount of care at the construction site helps. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable, caught by review after the arm shipped, three times. CEILING: mechanically preventable -- reachability of a coproduct arm from a named entry point is decidable over the same Node tree the namespace authority already reads, so a lens can compute, for each refusal cause, whether any path from the wet entry constructs it. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability and not an artifact: an arm-reachability reader over the acceptance closure that refuses a declared refusal cause with no constructing path, sufficient to run over a whole module's wet entries rather than one hand-named function. WHAT IS NOW HARDER TO DO THAN BEFORE: NOTHING. This filing is a RECORD and not a REPAIR, the class stands UNREMEDIED at mitigatable, and no reader may cite it as coverage -- see [[a_written_row_is_not_a_firing_mechanism]], whose obligation this row is discharging by saying so plainly rather than by implying a climb. THE ONE PRACTICE THAT DID FIRE, offered as the interim and not as the mechanism: mutate the guard and re-run the witness. A fixture-shaped witness stays green under `if false`; the three repairs above were each confirmed by a measured red at that mutation. DISTINCT FROM ITS NEIGHBOUR [[enforcement_gate_positioned_after_the_effect_it_guards]]: that one is about ORDERING AGAINST A SIDE EFFECT and its arm IS reachable, it is merely too late; this one is about CONSTRUCTOR REACHABILITY and its arm is never reached at all. Folding them would give one row two recognition rules, which is how a roster stops being usable.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
